<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christmas Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">January 1919</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Christmas Uprising was a revolt in Montenegro in early January 1919, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christmas, by supporters of independence and of the deposed King Nicholas I, known as the Greens. They opposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podgorica-assembly">Podgorica Assembly</a>'s decision of November 1918 to unite Montenegro with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. Serbian troops and local unionists suppressed the rising, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> resistance continued for several years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christmas-uprising.jpg" alt="Christmas Uprising" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adriano Minardi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borbe_kod_Podgorice_izme%C4%91u_crnogorskih_pobunjenika_i_srpske_vojske_1918..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
